WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.650
Claimant: Hi, I’m calling to report that an electrical surge damaged my laptop. It won’t turn on, and there’s a small scorched area beside the charging port; a technician confirmed the damage is confined to the internal circuitry.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:37.200
Adjuster: Decision: excluded. The claimant reports surge damage confined to the laptop’s internal circuitry, as confirmed by a technician. CA-HO4-CURRENT expressly excludes damage to circuitry within computers from the electrical-current peril; no material information gap remains. Next action: Issue a denial citing the computer circuitry exception in CA-HO4-CURRENT.
